{"h":3395,"lines":[{"h":0.013096803770750509,"c":1,"x":0.13168724375115445,"t":"Test 2","y":0.10174418590380141,"w":0.055555553436279298},{"c":1,"w":0.016460905075073251,"t":"F","y":0.405523255587388,"x":0.12962962966410946,"h":0.013081395583944833},{"x":0.13168724304868595,"y":0.56540697653319372,"w":0.018518517812093099,"c":1,"t":"G","h":0.013081395583944722},{"t":"The same is true in transport engineering, which uses models to predict and shape the","y":0.14389534868591902,"w":0.69135803222656245,"c":1,"x":0.16872427617752805,"h":0.015998644317698818},{"x":0.1727347816411707,"y":0.15980306334779759,"t":"way people move through the city. Again, these models are necessary, but they are built","w":0.70186075846354157,"c":1,"h":0.019718787976232388},{"c":1,"t":"on specific world views in which certain forms of efficiency and safety are considered","x":0.17275306377998068,"h":0.018240788238489514,"y":0.17667124562291803,"w":0.68946985880533851},{"w":0.6895464579264321,"c":1,"x":0.17065716131738412,"y":0.19240310663305427,"t":"and other experiences of the city ignored. Designs that seem logical in models appear","h":0.020391655192919966},{"t":"counter-intuitive in the actual experience of their users. The guard rails that will be familiar","h":0.018420144160869345,"c":1,"y":0.21001852099447693,"x":0.17275146666999983,"w":0.73268295288085938},{"c":1,"t":"to anyone who has attempted to cross a British road, for example, were an engineering","y":0.22471018479654614,"w":0.69379069010416661,"x":0.17060191248698062,"h":0.023869520081788553},{"w":0.72240768432617186,"h":0.019479630271453274,"t":"solution to pedestrian safety based on models that prioritise the smooth flow of traffic. On","c":1,"x":0.17068241292782829,"y":0.2430170989487882},{"t":"wide major roads, they often guide pedestrians to specific crossing points and slow down","y":0.26148409913291593,"c":1,"w":0.71399175008138016,"x":0.17283951580847354,"h":0.017667844522968101},{"h":0.020638792759116842,"y":0.27593853824587788,"c":1,"x":0.17268986380546855,"t":"their progress across the road by using staggered access points to divide the crossing into","w":0.71428899129231771},{"w":0.71011225382486987,"c":1,"y":0.29202090476156106,"h":0.020777055315752357,"x":0.17272242179766931,"t":"two - one for each carriageway. In doing so they make crossings feel longer, introducing"},{"w":0.71217219034830725,"h":0.0191787836548859,"x":0.17270933174137401,"t":"psychological barriers greatly impacting those that are the least mobile, and encouraging","y":0.31033762780383778,"c":1},{"h":0.024367727857034782,"c":1,"t":"others to make dangerous crossings to get around the guard rails. These barriers don't","x":0.17263632822360517,"y":0.3239839330658667,"w":0.68972127278645834},{"y":0.34291226110444861,"h":0.020160493075636943,"t":"just make it harder to cross the road: they divide communities and decrease opportunities","w":0.71833409627278644,"c":1,"x":0.17066057843016513},{"t":"for healthy transport. As a result, many are now being removed, causing disruption, cost,","h":0.017482947966235285,"x":0.17283951226942265,"y":0.36042402819862485,"w":0.71193415323893239,"c":1},{"x":0.17254657730868123,"y":0.38063231029115652,"w":0.091205145517985031,"h":0.014445817091439772,"c":1,"t":"and waste."},{"y":0.40230992254490883,"h":0.019675170574929512,"x":0.17273466819650782,"c":1,"t":"If their designers had had the tools to think with their bodies - like dancers - and imagine","w":0.72038899739583329},{"w":0.70184992472330732,"t":"how these barriers would feel, there might have been a better solution. In order to bring","x":0.17274527382206459,"c":1,"y":0.41929564596430224,"h":0.019271834859859283},{"t":"about fundamental changes to the ways we use our cities, engineering will need to develop","w":0.72655985514322918,"x":0.17273110307025299,"h":0.020074329892934673,"c":1,"y":0.43575308826843795},{"h":0.019947112659683519,"c":1,"t":"a richer understanding of why people move in certain ways, and how this movement affects","y":0.4528540400935972,"w":0.73066640218098944,"x":0.17274316558140118},{"h":0.017667844522968323,"x":0.17283949478105493,"c":1,"y":0.46937573596681847,"w":0.74074076334635408,"t":"them. Choreography may not seem an obvious choice for tackling this problem. Yet it shares"},{"h":0.017498356714686691,"t":"with engineering the aim of designing patterns of movement within limitations of space.","w":0.70781890869140629,"x":0.17489712994016324,"c":1,"y":0.48691860449066549},{"x":0.17283950821718463,"w":0.71193415323893228,"t":"It is an art form developed almost entirely by trying out ideas with the body, and gaining","y":0.50290697656965,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1},{"h":0.016019188192342826,"w":0.71193415323893217,"t":"instant feedback on how the results feel. Choreographers have deep understanding of the","c":1,"x":0.17283950789485147,"y":0.52031802124533233},{"y":0.53597987731055929,"h":0.020337058742419867,"c":1,"w":0.63811686197916673,"x":0.17474104049416306,"t":"psychological, aesthetic, and physical implications of different ways of moving."},{"y":0.56123244851729215,"w":0.72042984008789057,"c":1,"h":0.020938453180068151,"t":"Observing the choreographer Wayne McGregor, cognitive scientist David Kirsh described","x":0.17478509884516447},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"how he 'thinks with the body'. Kirsh argues that by using the body to simulate outcomes,","x":0.17489711989958409,"y":0.57979976452881532,"c":1,"w":0.71810699462890615},{"t":"McGregor is able to imagine solutions that would not be possible using purely abstract","x":0.17480123225522495,"y":0.59533783839825105,"w":0.69567769368489574,"c":1,"h":0.018824085329952167},{"h":0.020797446422779142,"t":"thought. This kind of physical knowledge is valued in many areas of expertise, but currently","c":1,"x":0.17479990430805412,"y":0.6106125640766682,"w":0.7368152872721353},{"h":0.019082598467176415,"y":0.62896983671973694,"t":"has no place in formal engineering design processes. A suggested method for transport","x":0.17276823865502591,"w":0.69975967407226569,"c":1},{"w":0.66274510701497391,"y":0.64556024020378511,"c":1,"x":0.17480168279353941,"t":"engineers is to improvise design solutions and get instant feedback about how they","h":0.018810552477977027},{"y":0.66138318008123387,"c":1,"t":"would work from their own experience of them, or model designs at full scale in the way","h":0.021286520716439106,"x":0.17477044423767571,"w":0.71221903483072913},{"w":0.730452677408854,"h":0.017462404653236896,"c":1,"x":0.17489711806750402,"y":0.68021201410283483,"t":"choreographers experiment with groups of dancers. Above all, perhaps, they might learn to"},{"w":0.39934015909830728,"h":0.017297812710100446,"t":"design for emotional as well as functional effects.","c":1,"y":0.69655073561471537,"x":0.17480568619153852},{"c":1,"y":0.92005813935786906,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.13374485607959105,"t":"38","w":0.024691357612609877}],"w":2400}